  "d083": "FAQ 18 and FAQ 5 give 'over 200 AWS services' and 'over 9,000 AWS API actions from over 200 services'; the FAQ itself says 'over 220 AWS services' in the generative AI use case line. These counts are not stored (FAQ numbers disagree with each other; the guide page supported-services-awssdk says 'almost any AWS service's API actions' without a count). The qualitative statements are stored.",
  "d085": "FAQ 9 gives Inline Map concurrency 40, 25,000 events or about 6,500 state transitions, and Distributed Map concurrency up to 10,000. Not stored from the FAQ: the numbers lens owns them and they must agree with service-quotas and state-map-distributed (the guide words 10,000 as the default number of parallel child executions, not a maximum). Qualitative Map facts stored.",
  "d091": "FAQ 27 says 'By default, Express Workflows report all outcomes to CloudWatch Logs'. The guide (cw-logs) says only an Express Workflow created in the console is configured to send logs by default; one created with the API, CLI or CloudFormation is not. Contradiction: the FAQ default-logging sentence is NOT stored; guide is current truth (behavior lens). Stored: 'Workflows that exhaust retries or have an unmanaged exception should be re-run from the start' (note on the fact)."
